FILE,LAD 2
SOR,0 XIC,I:1/1 BST,1 XIC,I:1/0 NXB,1 XIC,O:2/0 BND,1 OTE,O:2/0 EOR,0
RCM,Start/stop with seal-in. Start: NO on I:1/0. Stop: NC on I:1/1, so it is examined with XIC (not pressed = 1; a broken wire also stops). The O:2/0 contact holds the motor.
SOR,1 XIC,O:2/0 OTE,O:2/1 EOR,1
RCM,Running light while the motor is on.
SOR,2 XIO,O:2/0 OTE,O:2/2 EOR,2
RCM,Stopped light while the motor is off.
SOR,3 BST,1 XIC,I:1/2 XIC,I:1/3 NXB,1 XIC,I:1/4 XIO,I:1/5 BST,2 XIC,I:1/6 NXB,2 XIC,I:1/7 BND,2 BND,1 OTE,O:2/4 OTE,O:2/5 EOR,3
RCM,Combined logic: (I2 AND I3) OR (I4 AND NOT I5 AND (I6 OR I7)) turns on O:2/4 and O:2/5.
SOR,4 XIC,I:1/8 OSR,B3:0/0 OTL,O:2/8 EOR,4
RCM,Rising edge of I:1/8 latches O:2/8.
SOR,5 XIC,I:1/9 OTU,O:2/8 EOR,5
RCM,I:1/9 unlatches O:2/8.
SOR,6 END,6
RCM,
SYMBOLS
I:1/0 Start (NO)
I:1/1 Stop (NC)
O:2/0 Motor
O:2/1 Running
O:2/2 Stopped
